patch type="fixed" "Fix a track subscribed after a local unpublish not playing in single peer connection mode. Offers rewrote `a=inactive` to `a=recvonly` on every RTP section, including the one left behind by an unpublish, whose transceiver `removeTrack` has stopped — so the server could bind a remote track to a section that can never receive. The rewrite was ported from rust-sdks, where it compensated for passing libwebrtc's legacy `offerToReceive` option as 0; this SDK never passes that option, so receive-only transceivers already offer `recvonly` without it"
